# One shared scale: `ν Johnson.TridiminishedIcosahedron.polyhedron`

`johnsonTridiminishedIcosahedron_nu_shared_list`: **every system of `johnsonTridiminishedIcosahedron_nu_roots_list` has its one root at the scale
`ν Johnson.TridiminishedIcosahedron.polyhedron`** (`PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq`, `Modules/System/PolyRootEq.lean`): it is the one system. `johnsonTridiminishedIcosahedron_nu_reps_list`:
the same for the same system, and `johnsonTridiminishedIcosahedron_nu_reps` the statement in Mathlib's terms alone (`IsPolyRootEq`):
`ν Johnson.TridiminishedIcosahedron.polyhedron` is the first coordinate of the root of each of these systems, each with exactly one root in its
box; it implies `IsPolyRootMax` (`IsPolyRootEq.isPolyRootMax`). There is one system (`PolynomialSystem.IsRootMax.isRootEq_singleton`).
Generated by `lean/scripts/exact_n.py` from the theorems of `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandJohnsonTridiminishedIcosahedron`, `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandJohnsonTridiminishedIcosahedron.Exact` and
`Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandJohnsonTridiminishedIcosahedron.Roots`, which it does not change.
-/

